-- title:
--   Derived series of a subgroup, pairwise coverage by tuple monoids, and the augmentation kernel of a free group
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group. For an index set $\iota$, the set $G^\iota$ of tuples $z=(z_i)_{i\in\iota}$ is a group under coordinatewise multiplication. The file introduces the following notions.
--
--   1. **Derived series of a subgroup.** For a subgroup $N\le G$ define recursively
--   $$N^{(0)}=N,\qquad N^{(n+1)}=\bigl[N^{(n)},N^{(n)}\bigr]\quad(n\ge 0),$$
--   where $[A,B]$ is the subgroup generated by the commutators $xyx^{-1}y^{-1}$ with $x\in A$, $y\in B$. If $N$ is normal in $G$, then every $N^{(n)}$ is normal in $G$.
--   2. **Pair coverage.** A submonoid $M\le G^\iota$ *covers the subgroup $N\le G$ in pairs* if for any two distinct indices $i\ne j$ and any $a,b\in N$ there is $z\in M$ with $z_i=a$ and $z_j=b$. Equivalently, for every pair $i\ne j$ the image of $M$ under $z\mapsto(z_i,z_j)$ contains $N\times N$.
--   3. **Restriction homomorphism.** For a map $f:\kappa\to\iota$, the monoid homomorphism $G^\iota\to G^\kappa$, $z\mapsto z\circ f$, which re-indexes a tuple along $f$ (a restriction to a sub-family when $f$ is injective).
--   4. **Augmentation of a free group.** For a set $X$ let $F(X)$ be the free group on $X$. The augmentation is the homomorphism $\epsilon_X:F(X)\to\mathbb{Z}$ (with $\mathbb{Z}$ written multiplicatively) sending every generator $x\in X$ to the generator $1$; thus $\epsilon_X$ of a word is its total exponent sum.
--   5. **Augmentation kernel.** $\Delta(X)=\ker\epsilon_X$, the normal subgroup of $F(X)$ formed by the words of total exponent sum $0$ (for instance all quotients $xy^{-1}$ of two generators).
--
--   These objects drive an induction on the number of coordinates: if a monoid $M\le G^\iota$ contains all constant tuples, admits inverses on every pair of coordinates and covers a normal subgroup $N$ in pairs, then $N^{(n)}$ lies in the group of single-coordinate fractions $uv^{-1}$ ($u,v\in M$) whenever $|\iota|\le n+2$. In the Euclidean Ramsey argument the subgroup $N$ is the augmentation kernel $\Delta(X)$ of the free group on the points $X$ of a Euclidean space.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `Derived N n` is defined by recursion with `⁅_,_⁆`, and the instance `derived_normal` gives normality. `PairCoverage M N` and `restrictionHom f` are stated for `M : Submonoid (ι → G)`. `freeAugmentation X : FreeGroup X →* Multiplicative ℤ` is `FreeGroup.lift (fun _ => Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)`, and `AugKernel X` is its kernel, with an instance recording normality.
